  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted) achieved 0.523 acc, only modestly above RNA-only pca_n2000 (0.485), while image-only resnet50 was very weak (0.208). This suggests the image branch may be a bottleneck in the multimodal model. Question: Does replacing resnet50 with imagenet_vit_l (a stronger image encoder) improve multimodal performance? config_008 is identical to config_018 except for the image encoder, making it a clean single-variable A/B test that isolates the image representation effect. Why this is the best next step: Under a limited budget, resolving whether the image encoder is the limiting factor is the highest-value uncertainty. If imagenet_vit_l substantially lifts multimodal accuracy, it justifies investing further in image-heavy configurations; if not, we can focus budget on RNA encoder and profile/aggregation choices instead. This avoids the risk of prematurely exploring multiprofile or fusion variants on top of a weak image backbone."
